# shawndo site env for glm-v53-flash-nvfp4-tp4-switchless (stock nvidia NVFP4, zero weight mods).
# Bring-up copies this file to upstream/.env on the head (spark-0f0b) — upstream's .gitignore
# ignores .env, so the node tree stays pristine. Based on upstream .env.switchless.example
# @ pin 770d115. Values sourced from the FP8 glm-v53-flash-fp8-tp4-switchless recipe's committed site config.

# start.sh runs ON the head; rank 0 = local. Aliases resolve from spark-0f0b's SSH mesh.
HOSTS="local spark-6d14.shawndo.intra spark-6d90.shawndo.intra spark-6d24.shawndo.intra"
SSH_OPTS="-o BatchMode=yes"
# Management LAN, rank order 0..3 (same as the FP8 recipe's cluster map).
# 2026-10-19 move: the cluster's wired mgmt NIC enP7s7 is DOWN at the new location;
# mgmt/bootstrap runs over the wireless NIC wlP9s9 (10.69.43.0/16). DNS updated.
IPS="10.69.43.170 10.69.43.171 10.69.43.172 10.69.43.173"
# Bootstrap/mgmt interface for the launcher's socket env (NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME,
# GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME, MN_IF_NAME, TP_SOCKET_IFNAME): must reach ALL ranks — the mgmt
# NIC wlP9s9 (10.69.43.0/16, wireless). NOT a fabric PF: enp1s0f0np0 etc. live on
# per-link /24s and can only reach that link's single peer. (enP7s7 is the wired
# mgmt NIC — DOWN at the new site; switch FABRIC_IFACE back if it returns.)
FABRIC_IFACE=wlP9s9
# PHASE E (research.md changelog 2026-10): full four-PF contract. Every 200G cable
# presents TWO PFs — left port enp1s0f0np0/rocep1s0f0 + enP2p1s0f0np0/roceP2p1s0f0,
# right port the f1 equivalents — and the four-PF build needs an address on the second
# PCIe view (enP2p1s0f*) of every link. Netplan: each cable's /24 carries one extra
# address per node on the P2 view (map in research.md; additive over the FP8 plan, so
# the FP8 lane's 2-PF addressing is untouched).
IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0,rocep1s0f1,roceP2p1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f1
# Site four-PF NCCL build (othexmr/switchless-nccl @ 94c2669 + one-line site GID patch,
# site/nccl-4pf/, research.md "NCCL four-device verdict" entry). Deliberately a SEPARATE
# directory from the FP8 lane's ~/.local/lib/nccl-patched (SHA afe5f486…): the four-PF
# lib's hardened switchless path is triggered by NCCL_SKIP_TREE_CONNECT alone and
# rejects NCCL_IB_MERGE_NICS != 0, which the FP8 launcher (2 PFs, default merged vdev)
# would hit on its next boot. Rollback: point NCCL_HOST_DIR back at nccl-patched and
# re-apply the staged-transport mods (see upstream/scripts/transport.sh comment).
NCCL_HOST_DIR="$HOME/.local/lib/nccl-patched-4pf"
SWITCHLESS_NCCL_SHA256=8de68def30bcde20fabded468bd60f0df82ea12d3ead02d5120c7feda7a41a87
# Site ring: 4 QSFP56 cables × 2 PFs each = 8 logical /24 links (FP8 recipe used only 4).
# 10.10.0.0/21 covers 10.10.0.x–10.10.7.x; per-link addressing is the netplan map in
# research.md (additive over the FP8 plan). NOTE: othexmr's four-PF build was validated
# on 10.100.224.0/22 — the site rebuild re-pins tp4ValidateListener's GID range to
# 10.10.1–4 (site/nccl-4pf/nccl-2.30.7-dual-pf.site.patch) and requires its own gates.
SWITCHLESS_ADDR_RANGE=10.10.0.0/21
SWITCHLESS_SUBNET_PREFIX_LEN=24
TRANSPORT=switchless
# Built from Dockerfile.roce on every node per upstream docs/install.md (minutes, no CUDA compile).
IMAGE=glm53-roce:v11-b58f34ea
# Materialized real directories (hardlinks into the HF cache blobs — zero copy, zero
# weight modification). Created by ../site/materialize-weights.sh on every node.
MODEL_DIR="$HOME/.local/nvfp4-tp4/weights/nvidia-glm53-nvfp4"
DRAFT_DIR="$HOME/.local/nvfp4-tp4/weights/glm53-dflash2"
CTN=glm53-nvfp4
OVERLAY_REMOTE="$HOME/.local/nvfp4-tp4"
# Site-added zero-mod profile (committed at upstream/profiles/stock-nvfp4.env).
source profiles/stock-nvfp4.env
